    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the datalink router rack installation, showing the ventilated tray and the plain tray as alternates and the shelf positions before and after the relocation.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "Illustrated parts breakdown of the air traffic control datalink router installation in the upper avionics rack, including the mounting tray alternates and the display interface unit position.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn looking aft at the rack face. The shelf position numbering on sheet 1 is the post-relocation arrangement; sheet 2 gives the pre-relocation arrangement, which is why a router removed from an unmodified aircraft does not come out of the position this figure shows. The alternates at item 10 are the ventilated and the plain tray. The vendor interface unit at item 30 is common to both standards and is not affected by the relocation."
    },
